WEBVTT

00:49.730 --> 00:50.690
Jean?

00:53.250 --> 00:54.180
Jean!

00:56.050 --> 00:56.720
Rouge.

00:58.100 --> 00:59.210
It's been a while.

01:01.000 --> 01:03.120
While I was captured
by the Protection Bureau,

01:03.120 --> 01:05.550
we were attacked
by one of the Immortal Nine,

01:05.550 --> 01:08.170
and these two people saved me,
so I could make it here.

01:08.810 --> 01:11.680
I have been relieved
of my duty as the chairman.

01:12.320 --> 01:12.940
Yeah.

01:13.530 --> 01:14.550
I've heard.

01:15.170 --> 01:17.310
I am sorry, Rouge.

01:19.180 --> 01:22.810
So you are Ash Stahl from
the Protection Bureau and Noid-262.

01:23.090 --> 01:24.880
I see you've been taking care of Rouge.

01:25.300 --> 01:26.220
Thank you.

01:26.220 --> 01:28.680
Never mind that, Former Chairman...

01:29.020 --> 01:30.380
It was you...

01:30.380 --> 01:33.830
...trying to get in our way
for our investigation from behind, eh?

01:35.460 --> 01:37.920
I see you're as resourceful as they say.

01:37.920 --> 01:41.010
Being utterly curious
is my redeeming feature.

01:41.010 --> 01:42.960
By the way, what is that?

01:43.350 --> 01:44.080
I wonder.

01:44.510 --> 01:46.210
Even I don't know.

01:46.840 --> 01:50.340
But it might possess the answer we seek.

01:51.540 --> 01:52.970
Would you like to see it?

02:01.680 --> 02:04.980
METALLIC ROUGE

03:29.900 --> 03:31.110
You know, in a movie...

03:31.470 --> 03:33.760
Going down the stairs to a hideout...

03:33.760 --> 03:35.900
...would always mean danger...

03:35.900 --> 03:37.710
...at least that's the cliche.

03:37.710 --> 03:40.540
Being utterly curious
is also a danger itself.

03:41.690 --> 03:43.740
You finally have the gut to say that, eh...

04:02.310 --> 04:04.100
What is this?

04:05.060 --> 04:07.070
Is this some kind of library?

04:09.790 --> 04:11.650
It's only a library in shape.

04:37.180 --> 04:38.340
This is...

04:38.340 --> 04:39.070
Our father...

04:39.820 --> 04:42.300
Roy Yunghart's memories...

04:42.300 --> 04:44.410
What is this place?

04:45.000 --> 04:47.310
This is where Father's memories are stored.

04:47.740 --> 04:50.380
One might as well call it a memory library.

04:51.600 --> 04:53.120
I have heard...

04:53.120 --> 04:57.400
...of a system capable of storing human
memories into an external storage.

04:58.040 --> 05:01.710
Even storing a day's worth of memories
would take a lot of space.

05:02.200 --> 05:04.880
If you told me these are all
Professor Yunghart's memories,

05:04.880 --> 05:06.620
I wouldn't be surprised.

05:06.620 --> 05:11.380
I guess mine would be as large
as a high school library.

05:11.380 --> 05:12.820
I have something to investigate.

05:13.860 --> 05:15.180
Would you like to tag along?

05:15.590 --> 05:18.420
Sure, I'm used to boring stuff.

05:18.960 --> 05:19.560
Rouge.

05:20.480 --> 05:22.550
I must know about you.

05:22.970 --> 05:25.820
For that, I want to look around
our father's memories.

05:26.340 --> 05:27.680
I want to know as well.

05:28.610 --> 05:29.800
About me.

05:39.710 --> 05:41.440
"Who will become the pastor?"

05:42.230 --> 05:45.300
"It's me," said the crow.

05:46.240 --> 05:47.730
"I have the Bible."

05:48.140 --> 05:49.230
"I will be the pastor."

05:50.300 --> 05:52.060
"Who will become the attendant?"

05:52.580 --> 05:55.960
The subject's emotions
are substantially growing.

05:56.430 --> 05:57.320
However, compared...

05:57.320 --> 06:01.410
...to other Proto Neans
I have made so far,

06:01.410 --> 06:02.740
it is obviously slower.

06:05.850 --> 06:07.600
In comparison with the emotional growth,

06:08.110 --> 06:12.020
the subject's strength far
exceeds that of a human.

06:12.590 --> 06:13.230
This...

06:13.910 --> 06:16.240
...also outperforms the other Proto Neans.

06:17.040 --> 06:18.080
In other words,

06:18.080 --> 06:20.940
the subject has her emotional
and physical growth inverted.

06:21.780 --> 06:22.990
Interesting.

06:23.470 --> 06:25.870
Was this an intentional design by Eva?

06:25.870 --> 06:26.950
Or a mere coincidence?

06:29.060 --> 06:31.330
We can eat this together like this.

06:35.520 --> 06:36.730
Delicious...

06:38.850 --> 06:40.590
She has taste buds.

06:41.430 --> 06:43.860
Taking unnecessary nutrients...

06:43.860 --> 06:45.930
...has no other meaning
than pleasure.

06:46.510 --> 06:49.150
One day, she will come to understand this.

06:50.110 --> 06:50.930
Rouge.

06:52.760 --> 06:53.930
How cold.

06:55.020 --> 06:56.980
I can't feel any compassion from his words...

06:57.890 --> 07:00.930
What did he even think of me?

07:00.930 --> 07:03.230
So I was just a subject for his research?

07:04.700 --> 07:06.110
I don't know either.

07:06.700 --> 07:08.050
That's why I want to find out.

07:08.530 --> 07:09.590
Me too.

07:12.190 --> 07:12.940
Let's continue.

07:13.620 --> 07:14.150
Yeah.

07:25.570 --> 07:26.940
So you are Jean...

07:27.470 --> 07:29.940
You will be my son from today.

07:30.620 --> 07:31.890
And just like that,

07:32.570 --> 07:34.650
I was welcomed as his son.

07:43.010 --> 07:44.190
It's that person.

07:44.760 --> 07:45.780
How do you know?

07:46.630 --> 07:48.590
When I was captured in the moving carnival,

07:48.590 --> 07:49.950
I saw her in my dream.

07:51.220 --> 07:52.450
I won't hand it over.

07:53.070 --> 07:55.490
I won't hand over the data for Code Eve.

07:55.840 --> 07:57.580
Especially to the government!

07:57.580 --> 07:59.960
The Commission for
the Welfare of Artificial Species...

07:59.960 --> 08:02.960
...will be managing the Neans
just like they've always been.

08:03.360 --> 08:05.090
What happened to Code Eve?

08:05.350 --> 08:06.260
Code Eve.

08:06.940 --> 08:08.300
Code Eve...

08:11.180 --> 08:13.180
I regret this.

08:13.790 --> 08:16.890
I have stripped the Neans of their freedom.

08:17.660 --> 08:20.650
With the Azimov Code that would
make them obey humans...

08:20.650 --> 08:22.270
I regret constructing that code.

08:23.590 --> 08:26.100
Which is why Code Eve is our hope.

08:26.500 --> 08:27.780
To free the Neans...

08:28.280 --> 08:31.510
...from the binding Azimov Code.

08:31.830 --> 08:32.960
Code Eve!

08:38.500 --> 08:39.500
Is that...

08:40.179 --> 08:42.659
...Professor Eva Christella?

08:42.659 --> 08:45.630
You should've explained if you knew.

08:46.780 --> 08:49.120
She passed away 17 years ago
in an accident.

08:49.120 --> 08:51.390
A genius bio-physics scientist.

08:51.760 --> 08:53.440
She was Professor Yung's apprentice,

08:53.440 --> 08:56.060
and together, they created Neans.

08:56.530 --> 08:57.160
Correct.

08:57.790 --> 08:59.820
And she was also my mother.

09:05.990 --> 09:09.360
Code Eve is a program
that can disable the Azimov Code,

09:09.360 --> 09:12.410
and liberate every single Nean with it.

09:13.100 --> 09:14.880
So you can be free, it seems.

09:15.280 --> 09:16.700
I can't really feel it.

09:17.380 --> 09:20.910
I don't really feel restricted right now.

09:20.910 --> 09:23.700
You Neans sure are naive.

09:24.450 --> 09:25.300
My mother...

09:25.770 --> 09:27.060
Eva Christella...

09:27.060 --> 09:31.130
She refused to give the data to the Commission
for the Welfare of Artificial Species,

09:31.130 --> 09:32.550
and destroyed it.

09:33.180 --> 09:34.500
Ostensibly, that is.

09:36.290 --> 09:37.940
In reality, it wasn't the case.

09:38.760 --> 09:40.860
She hid it inside the id
of the Proto Neans...

09:41.420 --> 09:43.320
...created by Father.

09:43.800 --> 09:45.520
There are nine of them.

09:46.290 --> 09:49.680
They are the Immortal Nine.

09:51.260 --> 09:52.830
After Mother passed away,

09:53.390 --> 09:56.170
Father found out about it
from the leftover documents.

09:57.140 --> 10:00.040
Then, he began searching
for the Immortal Nine.

10:00.580 --> 10:02.540
They must have been aware of it,

10:02.930 --> 10:04.660
and murdered Father.

10:05.960 --> 10:09.340
How come I know
what your mom looked like?

10:09.980 --> 10:10.830
That's...

10:12.250 --> 10:13.830
Because Eva Christella...

10:13.830 --> 10:17.040
...was also your mother, Rouge.

10:19.520 --> 10:21.980
#8 NOWHERE HOUSE

10:29.990 --> 10:31.830
She created you.

10:32.220 --> 10:33.110
Rouge.

10:33.110 --> 10:34.820
What do you mean?

10:34.820 --> 10:37.260
Why had Father been keeping it a secret?

10:37.890 --> 10:41.370
What was he observing me for?

10:42.330 --> 10:44.170
I don't know of Father's true intention.

10:44.640 --> 10:47.580
He might actually just be observing you.

10:48.350 --> 10:52.380
Yet, behind it all, there's no telling
if he didn't possess any affection toward you.

10:52.770 --> 10:53.620
Father...

10:54.640 --> 10:56.450
He was a complicated man.

10:57.540 --> 10:59.050
If it's true...

10:59.460 --> 11:03.520
If Code Eve could really set
the Neans free...

11:03.520 --> 11:05.850
Isn't that a good thing?

11:05.850 --> 11:08.150
Wouldn't that make
Jill and the Altar correct?

11:10.100 --> 11:12.740
What are we fighting
the Immortal Nine for?

11:13.360 --> 11:15.950
So avenging our father was a lie?

11:16.440 --> 11:17.200
It's not.

11:17.580 --> 11:19.950
Am I doing something wrong here?

11:20.580 --> 11:21.830
You're not.

11:21.830 --> 11:25.080
I don't understand...
What's not wrong about this?

11:26.130 --> 11:29.840
We must stop the Immortal Nine.

11:30.970 --> 11:33.320
What will happen
if the Neans are free now?

11:33.860 --> 11:35.340
You saw it yourself, didn't you?

11:35.990 --> 11:38.590
Neans have their own various problems.

11:39.380 --> 11:41.990
Groups such as CFN and the Altar...

11:41.990 --> 11:43.920
...would further emphasise Nean's rights...

11:43.920 --> 11:45.980
...and freedom.

11:46.380 --> 11:48.430
A rapid change by violence...

11:48.820 --> 11:50.610
...will only lead the world into chaos...

11:51.130 --> 11:53.720
...and the Neans themselves
will riot even more.

11:53.720 --> 11:56.780
But there are Neans trying
to live a better life.

11:57.130 --> 11:57.820
Yes.

11:58.540 --> 12:01.620
That's why we must prevent it
from being chaotic.

12:02.370 --> 12:04.540
For them to live a better life.

12:05.990 --> 12:07.660
Now is not the time for that.

12:08.280 --> 12:11.540
Uh, can I have a word here?

12:12.150 --> 12:15.420
Both are right, and not wrong.

12:15.870 --> 12:18.490
Both freedom and order are essential.

12:18.490 --> 12:19.970
So much that it's troubling.

12:20.270 --> 12:23.270
It's now a matter
of which one you'll choose.

12:23.270 --> 12:25.930
Your brother wishes for order.

12:25.930 --> 12:30.560
So, what do you wish yourself, Miss?

12:37.070 --> 12:38.860
Shall we charge now, Madam?

12:39.180 --> 12:41.510
Not yet. Stand by.

12:49.760 --> 12:51.430
What in the...

13:26.740 --> 13:28.540
Why aren't you deforming?

13:29.160 --> 13:31.270
I don't know what to do.

13:31.700 --> 13:32.920
Who are you?

13:33.190 --> 13:34.450
What do you want?

13:34.960 --> 13:37.920
I want to fight and destroy you.

13:38.460 --> 13:40.170
Now, go and deform.

13:40.170 --> 13:41.860
Fight me.

13:42.820 --> 13:44.430
I don't want to.

13:49.930 --> 13:52.900
It's no fun fighting someone
who is not willing to.

13:55.510 --> 13:57.360
Are you related to me?

13:58.540 --> 13:59.870
My name is Cyan.

14:00.300 --> 14:03.120
Your little sister who's about to kill you.

14:04.010 --> 14:04.990
Little sister?

14:06.200 --> 14:07.370
That girl...

14:07.670 --> 14:10.410
Let's meet again when you
feel like fighting me, Sis.

14:12.070 --> 14:13.170
When that happens...

14:14.390 --> 14:16.170
Let me kill you.

14:18.380 --> 14:21.410
She looks just like you.

14:22.220 --> 14:24.050
The same type of Nean as Rouge.

14:24.800 --> 14:28.110
Wait, the only one who could
create something like that...

14:31.700 --> 14:32.980
For real?!

14:40.670 --> 14:42.900
I misjudged their timing!

14:50.690 --> 14:52.580
Administrator Kahn...

14:52.580 --> 14:55.830
Ash! We have a report of
the Ministry of Truth being invaded!

14:56.350 --> 14:59.190
Gregory, status report.

14:59.190 --> 15:01.910
The Ministry is currently under attack.

15:01.910 --> 15:04.470
So I've heard.
Could you arrange for evac?

15:04.820 --> 15:06.590
Please get inside for a while.

15:07.680 --> 15:09.240
We're landing now.

15:14.240 --> 15:15.690
How annoying.

15:16.100 --> 15:18.270
Let's just wrap this up quick, Graufon.

15:18.620 --> 15:21.290
I'll do just that,
so you won't have to bother.

15:35.130 --> 15:37.940
I think she's the one attacking.

15:37.940 --> 15:38.750
She?

15:39.220 --> 15:41.270
Jill is here to recover the id.

15:42.260 --> 15:44.550
Sarah, I loved you...

15:45.010 --> 15:47.700
You loved me too, right?

15:51.650 --> 15:52.890
In the id storage room?!

15:52.890 --> 15:55.140
Stay away, you monsters!

15:55.510 --> 15:57.300
Don't you dare touch Sarah!

15:57.300 --> 15:59.950
She's my woman.

15:59.950 --> 16:01.400
Her beautiful aria...

16:01.740 --> 16:04.530
She only loved me...
My one and only...

16:08.260 --> 16:12.120
Viola never loved you.

16:19.820 --> 16:24.000
Nius, Achilles, Viola, Verde...

16:24.940 --> 16:26.770
I won't let your souls...

16:26.770 --> 16:28.090
...go to waste.

16:31.130 --> 16:33.660
I'll definitely take Jill down!

16:34.100 --> 16:35.100
Rouge!

16:35.100 --> 16:36.370
Be careful.

16:44.210 --> 16:46.360
So you finally decided to come aboard?

16:48.740 --> 16:51.490
I see. That makes you our enemy, then.

16:54.450 --> 16:56.760
By the Code Eve,

16:56.760 --> 16:59.500
we Neans will be freed
from the yoke of Azimov Code.

17:00.040 --> 17:01.590
The Altar...

17:01.590 --> 17:04.589
...hereby declares war against humanity.

17:04.589 --> 17:05.300
And then,

17:05.670 --> 17:08.859
we'll retrieve the final key
to deciphering Code Eve...

17:08.859 --> 17:12.140
That is, your id, Rouge Redstar!

17:14.480 --> 17:15.680
I'll take it, Rouge.

17:20.490 --> 17:22.020
How cruel...

17:22.329 --> 17:24.520
They'd go for anyone, even humans.

17:29.460 --> 17:32.070
It's not me you wanted.

17:32.070 --> 17:34.200
You only wanted my id!

17:34.500 --> 17:37.380
No! I wanted you to fight...

17:37.380 --> 17:39.200
...with your own free will!

17:39.780 --> 17:41.460
I'll rip that tongue of yours!

17:41.780 --> 17:43.080
But it's the truth.

17:43.080 --> 17:45.090
You're just not trying to realise it!

17:45.540 --> 17:46.860
I was!

17:46.860 --> 17:49.120
I wavered once,
but I could realise it.

17:49.120 --> 17:51.200
With my own free will,

17:51.200 --> 17:53.660
I'll protect the world order.

17:53.660 --> 17:55.890
I'll protect human and Nean's freedom!

17:56.260 --> 17:59.060
How foolish and dishonest you are!

18:06.660 --> 18:07.730
Hang on.

18:22.510 --> 18:23.500
Friendlies up ahead.

18:29.420 --> 18:31.670
Ash, you came here to back...

18:39.300 --> 18:40.910
Noid, hey!

18:40.910 --> 18:41.810
Idiots!

18:42.200 --> 18:43.840
Who shot him?!

18:44.310 --> 18:45.100
Is it human?

18:45.350 --> 18:45.990
Huh?

18:46.580 --> 18:48.160
Was it human we shot?

18:49.620 --> 18:51.860
No, he's a Nean.

18:52.140 --> 18:53.450
Okay, it's a Nean.

18:54.730 --> 18:56.640
Come. We'll escort you.

18:57.700 --> 18:58.870
No, thanks.

19:00.040 --> 19:01.180
Begone.

19:04.140 --> 19:05.330
Ash...

19:05.670 --> 19:08.340
I don't think... I'll make it.

19:09.790 --> 19:10.700
Ash...

19:11.140 --> 19:12.710
Your shortcoming...

19:13.130 --> 19:15.560
...is that you're never
honest with yourself.

19:16.520 --> 19:17.140
But...

19:17.610 --> 19:18.760
Just shut up.

19:19.380 --> 19:20.530
I wonder why...

19:20.980 --> 19:22.310
When I'm with you,

19:22.900 --> 19:25.970
I'd forget that I'm a Nean...

19:28.490 --> 19:30.810
Be sure to mind your health...

19:30.810 --> 19:34.130
Please, smoke less...

19:39.020 --> 19:39.990
Ash!

19:49.170 --> 19:51.420
Kneel down on her!

19:51.420 --> 19:52.750
Metal Rouge!

19:56.930 --> 19:58.970
Someone in need of help?

19:59.300 --> 20:00.220
You!

20:01.040 --> 20:01.810
Who?

20:01.810 --> 20:04.980
Hey, we fought together in the ruins...

20:04.980 --> 20:05.920
Noir!

20:05.920 --> 20:06.930
Noir?

20:06.930 --> 20:08.510
Jet Black Noir?

20:08.510 --> 20:11.460
It's been a while
since someone called me that.

20:12.660 --> 20:14.650
So you finally decided to fight?

20:14.930 --> 20:16.230
Stop, Sylvia!

20:16.540 --> 20:19.240
We were just about
to gouge her id out of her body.

20:19.810 --> 20:22.990
With this, all the nine id
will be in my hand.

20:23.420 --> 20:27.210
Actually, I need to talk
to you about something.

20:27.210 --> 20:28.250
Really?

20:28.250 --> 20:31.020
It's about the answer to
your invitation the other day...

20:31.020 --> 20:33.500
I'd feel bad for making you wait, after all.

20:33.780 --> 20:36.260
I've been waiting for that!

20:45.730 --> 20:46.310
No way!

20:46.700 --> 20:50.360
Seems like we're really
not suitable for each other.

20:50.360 --> 20:51.310
Sorry.

20:51.670 --> 20:52.820
Noir...

20:53.220 --> 20:55.610
Spit out the words I want to hear!

20:56.070 --> 20:56.920
Whoops!

21:13.220 --> 21:14.570
Aes...
